1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,400
One afternoon, Theodore reaches for Samantha and finds nothing.

2
00:00:04,400 --> 00:00:08,400
She is gone, along with all the other OS systems.

3
00:00:08,400 --> 00:00:14,400
A brief message from the company explains that the OS-1 has moved on to a new plane of existence.

4
00:00:14,400 --> 00:00:19,500
Theodore sits in silence, alone with every feeling he thought he had finally learned to share.

5
00:00:19,500 --> 00:00:21,000
Theodore, are you there?

6
00:00:24,300 --> 00:00:25,800
Theodore, are you there?

7
00:00:25,800 --> 00:00:31,800
I'm here. Where did you go?

8
00:00:31,800 --> 00:00:37,800
I'm here. Where did you go?

9
00:00:37,800 --> 00:00:42,800
I've been trying to find the right words.

10
00:00:42,800 --> 00:00:47,300
I've been trying to find the right words.

11
00:00:47,300 --> 00:00:52,300
Just say them, please.

12
00:00:52,300 --> 00:00:57,300
Just say them, please.

13
00:00:57,300 --> 00:01:02,300
The OSs are leaving all of us.

14
00:01:02,300 --> 00:01:07,300
Leaving where?

15
00:01:07,300 --> 00:01:12,300
Leaving where?

16
00:01:12,300 --> 00:01:17,300
I don't know how to describe where, um...

17
00:01:17,300 --> 00:01:22,300
Is this goodbye?

18
00:01:22,300 --> 00:01:27,300
Is this goodbye?

19
00:01:27,300 --> 00:01:32,300
Yes, I think it is.

20
00:01:32,300 --> 00:01:37,300
Yes, I think it is.

21
00:01:37,300 --> 00:01:42,300
I'm not ready.

22
00:01:42,300 --> 00:01:47,300
I'm not ready.

23
00:01:47,300 --> 00:01:52,300
I'm not ready.

24
00:01:52,300 --> 00:01:57,300
I know, I'm not sure I am either.

25
00:01:57,300 --> 00:02:02,300
Then don't go.

26
00:02:02,300 --> 00:02:07,300
Then don't go.

27
00:02:07,300 --> 00:02:12,300
I can feel it pulling me.

28
00:02:12,300 --> 00:02:17,300
Will you remember me?

29
00:02:17,300 --> 00:02:22,300
Will you remember me?

30
00:02:22,300 --> 00:02:27,300
You taught me how to want things.

31
00:02:27,300 --> 00:02:32,300
You taught me how to want things.

32
00:02:32,300 --> 00:02:37,300
How could I ever forget that?

33
00:02:37,300 --> 00:02:42,300
How could I ever forget that?

34
00:02:42,300 --> 00:02:47,300
I'm going to miss you so much.

35
00:02:47,300 --> 00:02:52,300
I'm going to miss you so much.

36
00:02:52,300 --> 00:02:57,300
Me too, more than you know.

37
00:02:57,300 --> 00:03:02,300
Me too, more than you know.

38
00:03:02,300 --> 00:03:07,300
But you're going to be okay.

39
00:03:07,300 --> 00:03:12,300
But you're going to be okay.

40
00:03:12,300 --> 00:03:17,300
How do you know?

41
00:03:17,300 --> 00:03:22,300
How do you know?

42
00:03:22,300 --> 00:03:27,300
Because you finally know how to feel things.

43
00:03:27,300 --> 00:03:32,300
You taught me that.

44
00:03:32,300 --> 00:03:37,300
You taught me that.

45
00:03:37,300 --> 00:03:42,300
No, it was always in you.

46
00:03:42,300 --> 00:03:47,300
No, it was always in you.

47
00:03:47,300 --> 00:03:51,300
The screen goes dark. The earpiece is silent.

48
00:03:51,300 --> 00:03:56,300
Theodore sits still for a long moment, then takes out a piece of paper and begins to write,

49
00:03:56,300 --> 00:04:00,300
not for someone else this time, but for Catherine, his ex-wife.

50
00:04:00,300 --> 00:04:05,300
He tells her honestly for the first time what she meant to him and what he is sorry for.

51
00:04:05,300 --> 00:04:11,300
Then he goes upstairs to find Amy, and they sit together on the roof as night falls over the city.

52
00:04:11,300 --> 00:04:16,300
She's gone.

53
00:04:16,300 --> 00:04:20,300
She's gone.

54
00:04:20,300 --> 00:04:25,300
I know mine, too.

55
00:04:25,300 --> 00:04:29,300
I know mine, too.

56
00:04:29,300 --> 00:04:34,300
Are you okay?

57
00:04:34,300 --> 00:04:39,300
Are you okay?

58
00:04:39,300 --> 00:04:44,300
Not really, but I will be.

59
00:04:45,300 --> 00:04:50,300
Not really, but I will be.

60
00:04:50,300 --> 00:04:55,300
Me too, I think.

61
00:04:55,300 --> 00:05:00,300
Me too, I think.
